e it:\n- Develops a piece toward the center\n- Attacks the e4 square, preventing White from easily establishing a pawn there\n- Prepares for kingside castling (after developing the f8 bishop)\n- Follows opening principles: knights before bishops\n- Is the most flexible move that keeps all options open\n- Aligns with classical opening theory in this position\n\nAnswer: N: g8-f6"}
