lable in the opening/early middlegame, especially when the opponent's king is still in the center. This move simultaneously improves king safety and connects my rooks.\n\nReason: White's king is still in the center on e1, making it vulnerable. By castling kingside, I secure my king's safety, connect my rooks, and bring my h8 rook into potential play. This is a fundamental principle - castle early to protect the king and activate rooks. Given that my development is reasonable and White hasn't castled, getting my king to safety is the priority.\n\nAnswer: K: e8-g8"}
