ing itself. This forces White to respond to the threat immediately (likely g2-g3 or Qd1-e2), disrupting White's development plans and allowing Black to seize the initiative. In a position where White has better piece activity, creating immediate tactical threats is crucial.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-h4"}
