se it centralizes my rook on the e-file, pointing directly at White's awkwardly placed king on f2. This move improves my piece coordination, maintains flexibility for future plans, and puts subtle pressure on White's exposed king position. It's a principled developing move that keeps all my options open while improving my position.\n\n**Answer:** R: f8-e8"}
